Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:56:31 +0800
Subject: power: reset: syscon-reboot: Use devm_register_sys_off_handler(RESTART)

The driver registers its restart handler with
register_restart_handler() but never unregisters it: there is no
remove callback and the notifier block lives in the devm-allocated
context. Once the device is unbound (e.g. through sysfs), the freed
notifier stays on the restart handler list. The list is walked in
descending priority order, so the dangling entry, registered with
syscon-reboot's default priority of 192, is hit before any handler
with a lower priority: the next reboot oopses on the stale entry and
the working handlers behind it never run.

Use the device-managed sys-off handler registration, which
unregisters the handler on driver unbind. The priority configured from
DT keeps its previous meaning. This mirrors the conversion of the
syscon-poweroff sibling.

Fixes: 09fb07bcaf52 ("power: reset: Add generic SYSCON register mapped reset")
Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)


diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/syscon-reboot.c b/drivers/power/reset/syscon-reboot.c
index 60e855cae68e..348a9550e9e3 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/syscon-reboot.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/syscon-reboot.c
@@ -31,16 +31,12 @@ struct syscon_reboot_context {
 
 	const struct reboot_data *rd; /* from of match data, if any */
 	struct reboot_mode_bits catchall; /* from DT */
-
-	struct notifier_block restart_handler;
 };
 
-static int syscon_restart_handle(struct notifier_block *this,
-					unsigned long mode, void *cmd)
+static int syscon_restart_handle(struct sys_off_data *data)
 {
-	struct syscon_reboot_context *ctx =
-			container_of(this, struct syscon_reboot_context,
-					restart_handler);
+	struct syscon_reboot_context *ctx = data->cb_data;
+	unsigned int mode = data->mode;
 	const struct reboot_mode_bits *mode_bits;
 
 	if (ctx->rd) {
@@ -113,11 +109,11 @@ static int syscon_reboot_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
-	ctx->restart_handler.notifier_call = syscon_restart_handle;
-	ctx->restart_handler.priority = priority;
-	err = register_restart_handler(&ctx->restart_handler);
+	err = devm_register_sys_off_handler(dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
+					    priority, syscon_restart_handle,
+					    ctx);
 	if (err)
-		dev_err(dev, "can't register restart notifier (err=%d)\n", err);
+		dev_err(dev, "can't register restart handler (err=%d)\n", err);
 
 	return err;
 }
